WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.320
- [Joe] My dog's name is Bubbles.

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:02.153
- [Kelly] Bubbles.

00:00:02.153 --> 00:00:03.300
- Yeah, and

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:05.910
she's very protective of Da-da.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:07.170
- Oh, my dog Henry is like that.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:08.670
- Yeah, she'll jump

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:09.649
at you.

00:00:09.649 --> 00:00:11.125
- Okay, my.
- If you're near Da-da.

00:00:11.125 --> 00:00:12.060
- Okay, mine doesn't do that.

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.830
- Okay.
- Yeah.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:14.790
Mine just kind of growls.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:15.990
- We'll keep a little distance.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:16.823
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- For right now.

00:00:16.823 --> 00:00:17.656
- [Kelly] Keep a little distance.

00:00:17.656 --> 00:00:18.489
- Just a little bit.

00:00:18.489 --> 00:00:19.620
- [Kelly] Warm her up.
Get to know my voice.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.453
- [Joe] Yeah.

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:21.570
- The rhythm of Kelly.
(Joe laughs lightly)

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.640
Well, let's get her comfortable
with the rhythm of Kelly.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.560
Wait, which one does she
like more, you or Sophia?

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.393
- Me.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:27.226
- I love that.

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:28.200
- Yeah, no question.
- It's like a big

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.700
giant dude with a little dog.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:30.540
It's so great.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.250
- She wanted the dog,
but the dog wanted me.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.080
She was a rescue, so.
- Oh, I love that.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.540
- You know, Sophia saw a picture of her

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.717
and was like, oh my gosh,
she is the cutest dog ever.

00:00:38.717 --> 00:00:39.550
- [Kelly] She is.

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:40.980
- [Joe] So the shelter brought her over.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:42.270
And as soon as she saw me,

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:43.860
she came running over.
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:44.693
And that was it.

00:00:44.693 --> 00:00:46.530
And then she started
growling at Sophia to go away

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:47.880
and growling at the shelter people.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:48.930
I'd never had a pet before.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:50.040
- And you were like, we'll take her.

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.554
- I said, well, I never had a pet.

00:00:51.554 --> 00:00:52.735
I said.

00:00:52.735 --> 00:00:53.568
- You never had a pet?

00:00:53.568 --> 00:00:54.840
- How do we do this?
Yeah.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:55.673
- Not as a kid?

00:00:55.673 --> 00:00:58.230
- No, and then I always
traveled and worked so much

00:00:58.230 --> 00:00:59.670
that it was just, it was ridiculous.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:01.080
I couldn't have a dog.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:03.570
So the shelter brought her over and,

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:06.060
you know, she actually,
it turns out, was sick.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.247
She was peeing blood.

00:01:07.247 --> 00:01:08.220
- [Kelly] Oh no.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.630
- And it turned out that she had a cyst

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.760
that they were worried might be cancer.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.096
So, you know, Sophia was like, well, why

00:01:14.096 --> 00:01:16.377
would they bring a sick dog
over without telling us?

00:01:16.377 --> 00:01:19.757
And I just said, look,
you know, if they told us,

00:01:19.757 --> 00:01:22.170
then nobody would ever have the dog over

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:23.460
and she'd never get adopted.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.140
So I just turned to the
shelter people and said,

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.120
look, I'll take her, whatever happens.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.127
- Look at that heart of yours.
- We'll figure it out.

00:01:29.127 --> 00:01:31.237
(crowd clapping)
- That's so cool.

00:01:31.237 --> 00:01:32.340
Because you have the means.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:33.540
- I would encourage people.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:34.710
Yeah, and that's the thing is like,

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:36.390
luckily she landed with
somebody who could,

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.890
you know, I could pay the medical bills

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:38.940
and whatever happened,

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:40.380
I was just gonna take
care of this little thing

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:41.213
and try to help.

00:01:41.213 --> 00:01:43.380
And you know, I try to
encourage other people because,

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:47.760
during Covid, a lot of people
went to shelters and got pets.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:48.593
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:48.593 --> 00:01:50.490
- And then as soon as the clouds broke,

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:51.810
and we started going back to normalcy,

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:53.970
those people brought the pets back.

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:56.700
So there's a huge number
of pets that have been,

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:57.630
that have been brought back.

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.220
- Special place in hell.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:01.080
- Seriously, seriously.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:03.000
- The nerve to walk back in,

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.170
you walk back in.

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:05.790
- Imagine taking this little thing back,

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:06.930
I couldn't imagine, so.

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.400
- [Kelly] I mean, I guess
I'm glad they brought it back

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.590
into the shelter and didn't
just let it go, I guess.

00:02:10.590 --> 00:02:11.423
- [Joe] Right.

00:02:11.423 --> 00:02:12.256
- But dang.

00:02:12.256 --> 00:02:13.089
- [Joe] Yeah, so people out there.

00:02:13.089 --> 00:02:14.400
- I love animals more than humans.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.304
- If you have the chance, like adopt,

00:02:16.304 --> 00:02:18.090
adopt a pet if you can.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:18.923
They're out there.

00:02:18.923 --> 00:02:20.205
They need homes like more than ever now.

00:02:20.205 --> 00:02:21.213
- [Kelly] Yeah.

